# Pinned runtime assets — the input contract for the S0.1 build.
#
# Every artefact that ends up in the APK is listed here with the hash it must
# have. The fetch script verifies against this file and refuses to continue on a
# mismatch, so a moved Termux index, a stale download or a tampered mirror
# cannot quietly change what runs on the phone.
#
# This file is EDITED BY HAND, and only deliberately: the hashes and the
# filenames below are what a report is allowed to claim it measured. When the
# Termux index moves, the fetch script says so and stops; updating a pin is
# a reviewed change, not a side effect of a build.
#
# The proot debs carry the versions in their names on purpose: a new proot is a
# new pin, because proot is the thing whose behaviour the spike measures.
#
# Format: sha256sum(1) format, checked with `sha256sum -c`. Paths are
# relative to the assets directory.

# proot and the two libraries it needs (Termux, aarch64)
0da3a24d558b93c92bcf8d611e0826a99ff96e396b148e6cdf33b47c47c57ff6  debs/libandroid-shmem_0.7_aarch64.deb
556591f43bb773ad8777e1a29522640866a55f95dab71914418b94a8c58ad5a7  debs/libtalloc_2.5.0_aarch64.deb
29de40efea4daa2a6168b617915206511c63e8d46bf5f4b07d48723441ef7f3b  debs/proot_5.1.107.98_aarch64.deb

# the glibc userland and the JS runtime
